-- title:
--   Polynomial and double-centralizer equalities for a cyclic multiplication operator
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $A$ be commutative semirings, let $A$ be an $R$-algebra, and suppose $x\in A$ generates $A$ by polynomial evaluation: every element of $A$ is $q(x)$ for some $q\in R[t]$.
--
--   Write $L_x\in\operatorname{End}_R(A)$ for multiplication by $x$, and let
--   $$C_x=\{T\in\operatorname{End}_R(A):L_xT=TL_x\}.$$
--   Then the following are equalities of $R$-subalgebras of $\operatorname{End}_R(A)$:
--   $$C_x=R[L_x],\qquad \operatorname{Cent}(C_x)=C_x.$$
--   Here $R[L_x]$ is the subalgebra generated by $L_x$, and $\operatorname{Cent}(C_x)$ consists of operators commuting with every element of $C_x$.
--
--   The statement allows trivial semirings and algebras and requires no field, finite-dimensionality, or polynomial-kernel hypothesis.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting algebra lemma for the Senthil Kumar mission, reusing polynomial_cyclic_centralizer_algebra (2ff7ad90-94c1-4594-a26a-05ecef737401), which in turn uses polynomial_cyclic_commutant (a572f240-2d39-4863-9c86-3b965e40549b). For a commutative R-algebra generated by x, the centralizer of multiplication by x is exactly the subalgebra generated by that operator and equals its own centralizer. The prior equivalence identifies the centralizer with the image of the regular representation; transporting adjoin along that homomorphism gives the polynomial algebra. Multiplication operators commute, and any operator centralizing the whole algebra centralizes its generator. Arbitrary commutative semirings and trivial algebras are allowed; no finite-dimensionality premise is needed. This is inferred supporting algebra, not a separately quoted theorem of the source article. Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474: Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval in RingTheory/Adjoin/Polynomial/Basic.lean; AlgHom.map_adjoin_singleton and Algebra.map_top in Algebra/Algebra/Subalgebra/Lattice.lean. Primary documentation: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Adjoin/Polynomial/Basic.html and https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Algebra/Subalgebra/Lattice.html . No new definitions.

import Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Adjoin.Polynomial.Basic

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.polynomial_cyclic_double_centralizer
    (R A : Type*) [CommSemiring R] [CommSemiring A] [Algebra R A]
    (x : A)
    (hx : Function.Surjective (fun q : Polynomial R => q.eval₂ (algebraMap R A) x)) :
    let C := Subalgebra.centralizer R
      ({Algebra.lmul R A x} : Set (Module.End R A))
    C = Algebra.adjoin R ({Algebra.lmul R A x} : Set (Module.End R A)) ∧
      Subalgebra.centralizer R (C : Set (Module.End R A)) = C := by sorry
